    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start on the high-level stuff. But for the actual boots-on-the-ground training, we need to get more specific. When officers are patrolling certain neighborhoods, they need to know what actually *looks* suspicious in real-time. \n\nCan you expand on that? Give me some more concrete examples of physical behaviors, ways of grouping up, or even specific ways of dressing/carrying oneself that tend to correlate with higher risk in these urban areas? I want to give them something tangible they can recognize immediately when they're on patrol.",
